-- P6 HARDENING / D1 (docs/EARTH-TILES-PLAN.md): FREEZE THE COUNTRY, NOT JUST THE CELL.
--
-- Migration 0053 froze every parcel's ADDRESS (`plots.earth_cell`) so that
-- regenerating the Earth data could not move land a minted deed already names —
-- the condition the owner's LOCKED Q3 decision ("the country goes on the deed")
-- was granted under. It was not sufficient, and the gap was found by an
-- adversarial pass on 2026-08-10: the deed still asked
-- `countryIdOfCell(EARTH_FINE, EARTH_COUNTRIES_FINE, cell)` PER REQUEST, and that
-- lookup is not a property of the ground. It resolves the cell to a RANK in the
-- fine mask's land enumeration (`landCellRank`), reads the country index at that
-- rank, and returns a 1-based id that is a position in an `ADM0_A3`-sorted list.
-- One land cell gained anywhere below a cell shifts every rank after it; one
-- feature added to Natural Earth renumbers every id. Either way the SAME frozen
-- cell would have printed a DIFFERENT country after a build step, and an on-chain
-- trait cannot be recalled.
--
-- So the answer is written down, once, next to the address it belongs to:
--   * `plots.country_a3` — Natural Earth `ADM0_A3`, the country's IDENTITY (and the
--     very sort key those ranks are ranks in, so it is what a renumbering cannot
--     touch). Written in the same INSERT as the plot from here on
--     (`tryAssignInValley`, apps/api/src/game/world.ts).
--   * `earth_countries` — that code's NAME, seeded here with all 240 features the
--     checked-in index carries, `NAME` verbatim (EARTH-TILES-PLAN R20: no flags, no
--     boundary this codebase redrew, no viewpoint it picked). The deed reads THIS
--     table, so the deed path imports nothing from the mask or the index at all.
--     Renaming a country is now a migration, which is what R15 asks of every fact
--     the Earth data feeds.
--
-- EIGHT STATEMENTS RATHER THAN drizzle's THREE, the shape 0044 / 0052 / 0053 all
-- use: a single `ADD COLUMN … NOT NULL` cannot succeed on a populated table, so it
-- is add nullable -> backfill -> assert nothing was missed -> tighten. Proven from
-- ZERO and against a populated `plots` before shipping.
--
-- MIGRATION-FIRST DEPLOY (0052's recorded rule, R18): the column is NOT NULL with
-- no default and the new API selects it unconditionally, so this ships before the
-- API. Old code against the migrated schema is safe — it simply never mentions
-- `country_a3`, and every INSERT it makes into `plots` would be refused, which is
-- the correct outcome for code that cannot state a parcel's country.
--
-- WHY THE CELL -> COUNTRY ATLAS IS EMBEDDED HERE AS DATA, exactly as 0053 embedded
-- the address book: `db:migrate` is `drizzle-kit migrate`, a pure-SQL runner with
-- no way to call into TypeScript, and a PL/pgSQL re-implementation of the country
-- vote would be a SECOND planet — the one bug apps/api/src/lib/globeGeo.ts exists
-- to prevent. So this carries the RESULT: every CLAIMABLE cell of the checked-in
-- 0.5° mask + country index, run-length encoded as [lo, hi] -> a3 over ascending
-- cell ids. MEASURED (2026-08-10, real code + the checked-in artefacts): 61,903
-- claimable cells in 3,991 runs, covering 61,903 cells exactly, 0 with no
-- sovereign, 170 distinct countries. apps/api/test/earth-address.test.ts re-derives
-- every run from `countryIdOfCell` and fails on a single difference, which is also
-- R15's freeze: regenerating the Earth is a migration, not a build step.
--
-- IT COVERS EVERY CLAIMABLE CELL, not only the 58,920 currently seatable ones
-- (120 patches x 491). The extra 2,983 cost ~7 KB of SQL and mean a future change
-- to how patches are streamed cannot leave this migration unable to address a plot.
--
-- 'ZZZ' IS "NO SOVEREIGN", AND IT IS REPRESENTABLE RATHER THAN A LIE. ISO 3166-1
-- reserves ZZ/ZZZ for user assignment, so it can never collide with an ADM0_A3
-- (asserted against all 240 features in the test). It is deliberately NOT a row in
-- `earth_countries`: a parcel whose cell has no sovereign gets NO Country trait
-- rather than a fabricated one, the same way a plot-less wallet gets no Location.
-- On Earth it is unreachable — claimable Earth is "land cells with a country" union
-- the sub-tile countries' cells, so every seatable cell has one, and the server now
-- REFUSES a seat rather than writing 'ZZZ' (game/world.ts). What it is really for
-- is a parcel on ANOTHER BODY: cell ids are mask-relative and this atlas is
-- Earth's, so a `planet_id <> 0` plot must not be handed an Earth country. The
-- backfill below is therefore scoped to planet 0 and everything else takes the
-- sentinel — which is why the column can be NOT NULL without lying about the Moon.
CREATE TABLE "earth_countries" (
	"a3" text PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
	"name" text NOT NULL
);--> statement-breakpoint
-- THE REGISTRY, all 240 Natural Earth admin_0 features from the checked-in fine
-- index, `ADM0_A3` -> `NAME` verbatim. Includes the 70 countries that own no
-- claimable tile at 0.5 degrees (owner decision D2, 2026-08-10: that is accepted and
-- documented, not engineered away) — a registry that only listed the countries that
-- happen to be seatable today would make "which countries exist" a function of the
-- patch stream.
