-- THE BACKFILL. `atlas` is the run-length-encoded cell -> country map; a plot's
-- `earth_cell` falls in exactly one run, or in none at all — which the next
-- statement catches loudly instead of leaving a NULL for `SET NOT NULL` to report
-- as "column contains null values". EARTH ONLY (`planet_id = 0`): cell ids are
-- mask-relative, so another body's cell is not an address in this atlas.
